{
  "version": "1",
  "_comment": [
    "STARTER vocabulary for inferring meaning from path segments when a file",
    "has no request-ID/flowcell match in metadata.csv.",
    "",
    "Copy to vocab.json (gitignored) and grow it from YOUR collection: the",
    "terms in your metadata's project, goal and project-type columns, and the",
    "abbreviations your folders actually use. Scripts prefer vocab.json when present.",
    "",
    "build_index.py stamps `version` onto every inferred association, so bump",
    "it on any edit and record what changed and why in this block. A refusal",
    "with no recorded evidence cannot be safely reversed later.",
    "",
    "Matching is case-insensitive against tokens split out of each path segment.",
    "Anything in 'ambiguous' is refused even if it matches: a too-vague token",
    "should not be interpreted at all. Add a term there when you MEASURE that it",
    "is often wrong on your collection (e.g. an abbreviation that is also a",
    "person's initials), and write the evidence here."
  ],
